    {
      "id": "jethro_0",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:1–5",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_0_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Jethro, priest of Midian and Moses' father-in-law, heard everything God had done for Moses and for Israel. He brought Zipporah and her two sons to Moses in the desert, near the mountain of God.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_1",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_1_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Moses went out to meet him, bowed down and kissed him. They greeted each other and went into the tent.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_2",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:10–11",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_2_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Praise be to the LORD, who rescued you from the hand of the Egyptians and of Pharaoh. Now I know that the LORD is greater than all other gods.",
          "position": "middle-right",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "jethro",
          "align": "right",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_3",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_3_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The next day Moses took his seat to serve as judge for the people. They stood around him from morning till evening.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_4",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:14",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_4_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "What is this you are doing for the people? Why do you alone sit as judge, while all these people stand around you from morning till evening?",
          "position": "middle-right",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "jethro",
          "align": "right",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_5",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:15–16",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_5_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Because the people come to me to seek God's will. Whenever they have a dispute, it is brought to me, and I decide between the parties.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "moses",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_6",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:17–18",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_6_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "What you are doing is not good. You and these people will only wear yourselves out. The work is too heavy for you; you cannot handle it alone.",
          "position": "middle-right",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "shake",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "jethro",
          "align": "right",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_7",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:21",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_7_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Select capable men from all the people — men who fear God, trustworthy men — and appoint them as officials over thousands, hundreds, fifties and tens.",
          "position": "middle-right",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "jethro",
          "align": "right",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_8",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Listen to Jethro and share the load ⚖️",
          "note": "Capable men judge the small cases. Only the hard ones come to Moses. The work becomes bearable."
        },
        {
          "label": "Keep judging every case alone 🕯️",
          "note": "The lines grow longer. Jethro's warning stands: the work is too heavy to carry alone."
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_8_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Moses had always carried every case himself. Now his father-in-law was asking him to share the weight.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ],
      "svg": "placeholder"
    },
    {
      "id": "jethro_9",
      "cite": "Exodus 18:24–25",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "jethro_9_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Moses listened to his father-in-law and did everything he said. He chose capable men from all Israel and made them leaders of the people.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
